---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "What is the main goal in IELTS General Training Task 1?",
    answer:
      "The main goal is to write a clear letter with the right tone, cover every bullet point, and make the purpose easy to understand from the start.",
  },
  {
    question: "How do I know if the letter should be formal or informal?",
    answer:
      "Look at who you are writing to and why. A letter to a manager or company is usually formal or semi-formal. A letter to a friend is usually informal.",
  },
  {
    question: "What lowers the score in IELTS Task 1 letters?",
    answer:
      "Students often lose marks when the tone is wrong, one bullet point is missing, or the paragraphs do not have a clear purpose.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "IELTS Writing Task 1 General Training Letter", path: "/blog/ielts-writing-task-1-general-training-letter/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="IELTS Writing Task 1 General Training Letter | Tone, Structure and Bullet Coverage"
  description="A practical IELTS General Training Task 1 letter guide with tone control, paragraph structure, and advice for covering every bullet point clearly."
  type="article"
  keywords="IELTS General Training letter, IELTS Task 1 GT, IELTS letter writing, IELTS writing Task 1 general"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section guide-article">
    <a class="guide-back-link" href="/blog">Back to blog</a>

    <header class="guide-header">
      <span class="guide-tag ic-eyebrow">IELTS writing guide</span>
      <h1 class="ic-display" style="margin: 0;">IELTS Writing Task 1 General Training letter</h1>
      <div class="guide-meta">
        <span>March 17, 2026</span>
        <span>7 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="guide-lead">
      <p>
        General Training Task 1 is practical writing. The best letters are easy to
        understand, use the right tone, and cover all the bullet points without sounding
        memorized.
      </p>
      <p>
        Many students know enough English to do well, but the score drops because the tone
        is wrong or one part of the task is missing.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-grid guide-grid-2">
      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2 class="ic-display">What a strong GT letter does</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>Makes the purpose clear in the opening.</li>
          <li>Covers every bullet point fully.</li>
          <li>Uses the correct level of formality.</li>
          <li>Ends with a natural closing line.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-card">
        <h2 class="ic-display">What often weakens the letter</h2>
        <ul class="guide-list">
          <li>The tone sounds too casual or too stiff.</li>
          <li>One bullet point gets only one short sentence.</li>
          <li>The letter has no clear paragraph plan.</li>
          <li>The opening is too long and indirect.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">A simple Task 1 letter structure</h2>
      <div class="guide-steps">
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Opening</h3>
            <p>Greet the reader and explain the reason for writing in the first one or two lines.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Body paragraph 1</h3>
            <p>Cover the first main bullet point clearly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Body paragraph 2</h3>
            <p>Cover the remaining bullet points in a logical order.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-step">
          <span class="guide-step__number">4</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Closing</h3>
            <p>End politely and use a sign-off that matches the tone of the letter.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">How to choose the right tone</h2>
      <div class="guide-example">
        <p><strong>Formal:</strong> Dear Sir or Madam, I am writing to express my concern about...</p>
        <p><strong>Semi-formal:</strong> Dear Mr. Ahmed, I am writing about the issue we discussed yesterday.</p>
        <p><strong>Informal:</strong> Hi Sara, I just wanted to tell you about something that happened last week.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-note" style="margin-top: var(--s-3);">
        <p>
          The relationship matters. Always ask yourself: Who am I writing to, and how well
          do I know this person?
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">The most important check before you finish</h2>
      <div class="guide-note">
        <p>
          Read the bullet points again. If the task gives you three things to include, make
          sure all three are easy to find in the letter. Missing one point can lower the
          score quickly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">Common mistakes</h2>
      <table class="guide-mistake-table">
        <tr>
          <th>Mistake</th>
          <th>Better move</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The opening sounds vague and indirect.</td>
          <td>State the purpose early and clearly.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The tone changes during the letter.</td>
          <td>Keep the same level of formality from start to finish.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>One bullet point is too short or missing.</td>
          <td>Check the task again before you finish.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>The closing sounds unnatural.</td>
          <td>Use a sign-off that matches the relationship and tone.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">Next step</h2>
      <div class="guide-links">
        <a href="/blog/ielts-writing-task-1-academic-guide">
          <strong>Read the Academic Task 1 guide</strong>
          <span>Compare General Training letter writing with Academic report writing.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ai-feedback">
          <strong>Try AI writing feedback</strong>
          <span>Find out whether your tone and bullet coverage are strong enough.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ielts/writing">
          <strong>Go to the IELTS writing hub</strong>
          <span>Move to Task 2 or the next writing lesson you need.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-card" style="margin-top: var(--s-4);">
      <h2 class="ic-display">FAQ</h2>
      <div class="guide-faq">
        {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
          <details class="card">
            <summary>{item.question}</summary>
            <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section-sm" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto; text-align: center;">
    <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #ddd; margin-bottom: var(--s-5);" />
    <p class="muted">Want a CLB 9 writing system you can actually follow?</p>
    <a class="btn" href="/celpip/writing">Get the system</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
